### ACMG-style criteria applied (candidate-level, provisional)
For each Tier A/B candidate, the pragmatic evidence codes below were considered. This is a
research assessment, **not** a formal clinical ACMG classification (which requires a qualified
laboratory, orthogonal confirmation, and — where applicable — functional and parental data).

| Code | Meaning | Applies here? |
|---|---|---|
| PVS1 | null variant in a LoF-mechanism gene | only for predicted-LoF candidates |
| PS2 | de novo (confirmed) | *partial* — de novo pattern seen, but father not sequenced (unconfirmed) |
| PS3 | functional studies show damage | not done — **recommended** |
| PM2 | absent/rare in gnomAD | yes for gnomAD-absent candidates |
| PP3 | computational evidence of damage | **strong** where AlphaMissense=likely_pathogenic, REVEL≥0.7, CADD≥25 all agree |
| PP4 | phenotype specific for the gene | yes (HIES phenotype ↔ panel gene) |

