## Limitations
- **Father not sequenced:** paternal alleles and compound-het phase are inferred, not confirmed; de-novo events cannot be distinguished from paternal transmission without paternal DNA.
- **Population frequency:** gnomAD allele frequencies were taken from the VEP cache; a genome-wide gnomAD v4 VCF was not available locally, so ancestry-specific (African) frequency filtering is limited — relevant for this family's ancestry.
- **In-silico:** genome-wide dbNSFP (REVEL/CADD/AlphaMissense) was unavailable; scoring relied on SIFT/PolyPhen and PhyloP. Final candidates should be re-scored with CADD/REVEL/AlphaMissense.
- **CNV:** exome CNV calls (CNVkit) with a 4-sample reference are sensitive to large events but require orthogonal confirmation (MLPA/aCGH), particularly for DOCK8.
- All Tier A/B variants are research candidates pending clinical-laboratory ACMG classification and orthogonal validation.

